{"key":"enterprise/T1580","id":"T1580","name":"Cloud Infrastructure Discovery","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["discovery"],"platforms":["IaaS"],"environments":["cloud"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"An adversary may attempt to discover infrastructure and resources that are available within an infrastructure-as-a-service (IaaS) environment. This includes compute service resources such as instances, virtual machines, and snapshots as well as resources of other services including the storage and database services. Cloud providers offer methods such as APIs and commands issued through CLIs to serve information about infrastructure. For example,…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1580","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--57a3d31a-d04f-4663-b2da-7df8ec3f8c9d","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.635Z","source_object_version":"1.3","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0017","name":"Cloud Storage Enumeration","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0017","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--fcc4811f-9cc8-4db5-8097-4d8242a380de","page":"telemetry/DC0017/"},{"id":"DC0075","name":"Instance Enumeration","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0075","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2a80d95f-08c4-48e3-833e-151ef19d90f5","page":"telemetry/DC0075/"},{"id":"DC0086","name":"Instance Metadata","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0086","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--45fd904d-6eb0-4b50-8478-a961f09f898b","page":"telemetry/DC0086/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0169","name":"Detection Strategy for Cloud Infrastructure Discovery","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0169","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--22331b2d-e8a1-4820-ae6b-7d04f24f7df7","relationship_id":"relationship--87f3ef36-2cfb-4707-96ea-650c60471651"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0481","name":"Analytic 0481","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0169#AN0481","guidance":"Defenders should monitor for suspicious enumeration of cloud infrastructure components via APIs or CLI tools. Observable behaviors include repeated listing or description operations for compute instances, snapshots, storage buckets, and volumes. From a defender’s perspective, risky activity is often identified by new or untrusted identities making discovery calls (e.g., DescribeInstances, ListBuckets, az vm list, gcloud compute instances list), enumeration from unusual geolocations or IPs, or rapid multi-service discovery in sequence. Correlating discovery API usage with later snapshot creation or instance modification provides further context of adversary behavior.","platforms":["IaaS"],"strategy_id":"DET0169"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0086","component":"Instance Metadata","name":"AWS:CloudTrail","channel":"DescribeInstances","platforms":["IaaS"],"analytic_id":"AN0481","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0169#AN0481","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0086/"},{"component_id":"DC0017","component":"Cloud Storage Enumeration","name":"AWS:CloudTrail","channel":"ListBuckets","platforms":["IaaS"],"analytic_id":"AN0481","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0169#AN0481","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0017/"},{"component_id":"DC0075","component":"Instance Enumeration","name":"AWS:CloudTrail","channel":"DescribeDBInstances","platforms":["IaaS"],"analytic_id":"AN0481","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0169#AN0481","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0075/"}],"unresolved_references":[],"basis":"ATT&CK detects relationship → detection strategy → analytic → log-source component reference","planning_inputs":[],"visibility":"source_mapped","planning_references":[],"references":[{"id":"DC0017","name":"Cloud Storage